R = {
"Korea creates Hangul alphabet": ("CS",2,"A Korean king invented an alphabet so simple that ordinary people could learn it in days.","Classical Chinese characters took years to master, so most Koreans couldn't read. King Sejong and his scholars designed Hangul, with letter shapes based on how the mouth forms each sound.","Elites resisted it for centuries, but it spread among women and commoners.","Korea has one of the world's highest literacy rates, and Hangul is a point of national pride."),
"Tumu Crisis": ("WP",2,"Mongols captured the Ming emperor, and China turned inward behind the Great Wall.","Emperor Zhengtong, urged on by a powerful eunuch, led a huge army north and was ambushed and captured by Oirat Mongols.","The Ming shifted to defense and rebuilt the Great Wall into the stone version we see today.","Most of the Great Wall tourists visit near Beijing dates from after this disaster."),
"Ottomans make Constantinople their capital": ("PR",2,"Mehmed II turned the fallen Christian capital into the heart of an Islamic empire.","Mehmed repopulated Istanbul with Muslims, Christians and Jews and turned Hagia Sophia into a mosque. He built the Topkapı Palace and the Grand Bazaar.","Istanbul became the capital of an empire spanning three continents for nearly 470 years.","Hagia Sophia's status, museum or mosque, is still politically charged."),
"Ōnin War → Sengoku era": ("W",2,"A succession fight burned Kyoto and plunged Japan into a century of civil war.","Rival samurai clans fought over who would follow the shogun. Kyoto was largely destroyed, and the shogun lost real power.","Local warlords fought each other until Japan was reunified around 1600.","The 'warring states' era is the setting for countless samurai films and games."),
"Vasco da Gama reaches India": ("EP",3,"Portugal sailed around Africa to India, opening the first sea link between Europe and Asia.","Vasco da Gama's ships took 10 months to reach Calicut. The pepper and spices he brought home were worth many times the cost of the voyage.","Portugal built a chain of forts from Africa to China and Europeans began dominating Indian Ocean trade.","Globalization by sea starts here; it's also the start of European colonialism in Asia."),
"Safavid Persia founded": ("RP",3,"A teenage shah made Shi'a Islam the faith of Iran.","Ismail I, about 14, united Persia and declared Twelver Shi'a Islam the state religion, sometimes by force, in a mostly Sunni land.","The Safavids fought the Sunni Ottomans for two centuries.","Iran is still the world's leading Shi'a power; the Sunni-Shi'a rivalry shapes the Middle East today."),
"Portugal takes Goa": ("PW",2,"Portugal captured Goa and made it the capital of its Asian empire.","Afonso de Albuquerque seized the port from the Bijapur Sultanate to control the spice trade.","Goa stayed Portuguese for 451 years.","India took Goa in 1961; its churches and food still show Portuguese influence."),
"Portugal takes Malacca": ("PWE",2,"Portugal seized the chokepoint of Asian trade.","Malacca, on the strait between Sumatra and Malaya, controlled ships between India and China. Albuquerque captured it in 1511.","The Dutch took it in 1641; the British in 1824.","The Strait of Malacca still carries about a quarter of the world's trade."),
"Suleiman the Magnificent": ("P",2,"Under Suleiman, the Ottoman Empire reached its peak.","Suleiman took Belgrade, Rhodes and Hungary, besieged Vienna, and issued a law code that earned him the name 'the Lawgiver'. His architect Sinan built mosques that still shape Istanbul's skyline.","After him, the empire stayed strong for a century but stopped expanding.","His reign is Turkey's golden age in popular memory."),
"Babur founds Mughal Empire": ("PW",3,"A Central Asian prince with cannons founded the Mughal Empire in India.","Babur, descended from both Timur and Genghis Khan, lost his homeland and turned to India. At Panipat his artillery beat a much larger Delhi Sultanate army.","His grandson Akbar built the empire into one of the richest in the world.","The Taj Mahal, Urdu and much of North Indian food and culture come from Mughal rule."),
"Portuguese guns reach Japan": ("SW",2,"Shipwrecked Portuguese traders brought guns, and Japan copied them fast.","A storm drove a Chinese ship with Portuguese aboard onto Tanegashima island. Japanese smiths reverse-engineered their muskets within a year.","Gun-armed armies helped warlords like Oda Nobunaga unify Japan.","Japan was producing perhaps more guns than any country in Europe by 1600."),
"Akbar the Great": ("PR",2,"Akbar built a vast, tolerant empire across most of India.","Akbar expanded the Mughal empire, abolished the tax on non-Muslims, married a Hindu princess and hosted debates between Muslim, Hindu, Christian and Jain scholars.","His successors kept the empire rich, though Aurangzeb later reversed his tolerance.","Akbar is held up in India as a model of religious pluralism."),
"Spain founds Manila": ("PE",2,"Spain founded Manila, linking Asia and the Americas for the first time.","Miguel López de Legazpi captured the port and made it the Spanish capital in Asia.","Manila galleons carried Mexican silver to China for 250 years.","The Philippines is Asia's most Catholic country, a legacy of Spanish rule."),
"Hideyoshi unifies Japan": ("PW",2,"A peasant-born general reunited Japan after a century of war.","Toyotomi Hideyoshi, who started as a foot soldier, defeated or won over every rival lord. He disarmed peasants and froze the social classes.","His death left a power struggle that Tokugawa Ieyasu won.","He's one of Japan's 'three great unifiers'."),
"Japan invades Korea": ("W",2,"Japan invaded Korea to reach China, and Korea's admiral sank its fleet.","Hideyoshi's armies took Seoul quickly, but Admiral Yi Sun-sin's armored 'turtle ships' cut Japanese supply lines, and Ming China sent an army.","Japan withdrew in 1598 after Hideyoshi died.","Admiral Yi is Korea's greatest hero; his statue stands in central Seoul."),
"Battle of Sekigahara": ("W",2,"One battle decided who would rule Japan for 250 years.","After Hideyoshi's death, Tokugawa Ieyasu's eastern army fought a western coalition. Key western lords switched sides mid-battle.","Ieyasu became shogun in 1603.","'Sekigahara' is still Japanese shorthand for a decisive showdown."),
"Tokugawa shogunate": ("P",3,"The Tokugawa family began 250 years of peace and isolation in Japan.","Ieyasu ruled from Edo (Tokyo). Lords had to spend every other year in Edo, keeping them loyal and broke.","Japan stayed peaceful and mostly closed to the West until 1853.","Edo-period culture, kabuki, woodblock prints, sushi, defines 'traditional' Japan."),
"Taj Mahal begun": ("C",2,"An emperor's grief produced the world's most famous tomb.","Shah Jahan built the white marble Taj Mahal for his wife Mumtaz Mahal, who died giving birth to their 14th child.","His son Aurangzeb later imprisoned him, and he spent his last years looking at the Taj from a window.","About 7 million people visit each year; it's the symbol of India."),
"Japan closes to the West": ("PR",2,"Japan shut its doors to the outside world for over 200 years.","Fearing Christianity and European influence, the shogunate expelled Portuguese traders, banned Christianity and forbade Japanese from leaving. Only the Dutch could trade, on a tiny island at Nagasaki.","Japan developed in isolation until US warships forced it open.","It explains why Japan modernized so suddenly and dramatically after 1868."),
"Ming falls; Qing dynasty": ("WP",3,"Rebels took Beijing, and Manchu invaders founded China's last dynasty.","Famine and rebellion broke the Ming; rebel leader Li Zicheng captured Beijing in 1644. A Ming general let the Manchus through the Great Wall, and they took China.","The Qing ruled for 268 years and doubled China's territory.","Today's China, including Tibet, Xinjiang and Taiwan claims, largely reflects Qing borders."),
"Kangxi Emperor": ("P",2,"China's longest-reigning emperor brought peace and expansion.","Kangxi ruled 61 years, crushed rebellions, took Taiwan, and studied Western science with Jesuit advisers.","Qing China reached its peak under him and his grandson Qianlong.","He's remembered in China as a model ruler."),
"Qing take Taiwan": ("PW",2,"The Qing conquered Taiwan, the root of Beijing's claim today.","Taiwan was ruled by Ming loyalists under the Koxinga family. The Qing navy took it in 1683.","Taiwan stayed part of the Qing empire until Japan took it in 1895.","Whether Taiwan is part of China is one of today's biggest flashpoints."),
"Aurangzeb dies → Mughal decline": ("P",2,"The last great Mughal died, and his empire broke apart.","Aurangzeb expanded the empire to its largest, but decades of wars against the Marathas and his religious intolerance drained it.","Regional powers rose, and the British East India Company exploited the divisions.","Aurangzeb is one of the most debated figures in Indian politics today."),
"Nader Shah sacks Delhi": ("W",2,"A Persian warlord looted Delhi and carried off the Peacock Throne.","Nader Shah crushed the Mughal army and massacred thousands in Delhi, taking the Koh-i-Noor diamond.","Mughal weakness was exposed to everyone, including the British.","The Koh-i-Noor is now in the British Crown Jewels and India still asks for it back."),
"Battle of Plassey": ("WPE",3,"A British company won Bengal, beginning British rule in India.","Robert Clive's East India Company army beat the Nawab of Bengal after bribing his commander Mir Jafar.","The Company took over Bengal's tax revenue and conquered most of India over the next century.","Plassey is often called the start of the British Empire in India."),
"China rebuffs British trade mission": ("PE",2,"China's emperor told Britain it had nothing China needed.","Lord Macartney arrived with telescopes and clocks to open trade. Emperor Qianlong wrote back that China had 'all things in abundance'.","Britain turned to selling Indian opium to China to pay for tea.","It's often taught as the moment China missed the industrial age."),
"Britain founds Singapore": ("PE",2,"A British agent picked a swampy island that became a global hub.","Stamford Raffles saw Singapore's location on the Strait of Malacca and made it a free port.","Singapore grew into the British Empire's key Asian port.","Singapore is now one of the world's richest countries per person."),
"First Opium War": ("WE",3,"Britain went to war to keep selling drugs to China.","China's Commissioner Lin destroyed 20,000 chests of British opium to stop mass addiction. Britain sent warships and crushed Chinese forces.","China signed the first of the 'unequal treaties' and ceded Hong Kong.","China calls this the start of its 'century of humiliation', a theme in its politics today."),
"Ottoman Tanzimat reforms": ("PI",2,"The Ottoman Empire tried to modernize to survive.","Sultan Abdülmecid promised equal rights for all subjects and reformed the army, schools and law along European lines.","Reforms angered conservatives and didn't stop nationalist breakaways.","The tension between Westernization and tradition still shapes Turkey."),
"Treaty of Nanjing": ("PE",2,"China gave up Hong Kong and opened its ports to Britain.","After the Opium War, China paid reparations, opened five ports and gave Britain Hong Kong 'in perpetuity'.","France and the US demanded similar treaties.","Hong Kong was returned in 1997."),
"Taiping Rebellion": ("WR",3,"A man who said he was Jesus's brother led a civil war that killed about 20 million.","Hong Xiuquan, after failing civil service exams, had visions and built a movement among the poor. His Taiping Heavenly Kingdom ruled much of southern China from Nanjing.","The Qing won only with regional armies and Western help, weakening central rule.","It's one of the deadliest wars in history yet little known outside China."),
"Perry's 'black ships' reach Japan": ("PE",3,"American warships forced Japan to open to the world.","Commodore Perry's steam-powered warships sailed into Edo Bay and demanded trade. Japan had no navy to resist.","Japan signed treaties, then overthrew the shogun and modernized rapidly.","Japan's transformation into a modern power begins here."),
"Indian Rebellion": ("WP",3,"Indian soldiers rose against the British, and Britain took direct rule.","Rumors that new rifle cartridges were greased with cow and pig fat outraged Hindu and Muslim soldiers. Revolt spread across northern India; both sides committed atrocities.","Britain abolished the East India Company and ruled India directly.","Indian nationalists call it the First War of Independence."),
"British Raj begins": ("P",3,"The British Crown took direct control of India.","After 1857, Queen Victoria's government replaced the Company. Viceroys ruled from Calcutta, later New Delhi.","British rule lasted 89 years, with railways, famines and English education.","India's railways, legal system and use of English are Raj legacies."),
"Summer Palace burned": ("W",2,"British and French troops looted and burned the emperor's Summer Palace.","During the Second Opium War, the troops destroyed the Yuanmingyuan palace complex in revenge for the torture of envoys.","China was forced to legalize opium and open more ports.","Its ruins are a national memorial in Beijing; China asks for the treasures back."),
"Meiji Restoration": ("PES",3,"Japan's samurai overthrew the shogun and turned Japan into a modern power in one generation.","Reformers restored the emperor and copied the best of the West: railways, factories, schools, a constitution and a modern army.","By 1905 Japan defeated Russia and was building an empire.","Japan became the first non-Western industrial nation, a model studied worldwide."),
"Japan forces Korea open": ("PE",1,"Japan used Western-style gunboat diplomacy on Korea.","Japanese warships provoked a clash and forced Korea to sign an unequal trade treaty.","Japan competed with China and Russia for control of Korea.","Japan annexed Korea in 1910."),
"Victoria made Empress of India": ("P",1,"Queen Victoria became Empress of India.","PM Disraeli gave her the title to tie India more closely to the Crown.","Famine struck in 1876–78 while celebrations went on.","The title lasted until 1947."),
"Indian National Congress": ("P",3,"Educated Indians formed the party that would lead India to independence.","Lawyers and teachers met in Bombay to press for a greater Indian voice in government.","Under Gandhi and Nehru, Congress led the mass movement for independence.","It ruled India for most of its first 50 years of independence."),
"French Indochina": ("PW",2,"France took Vietnam, Cambodia and Laos.","France conquered the region over decades and combined it into a colonial federation.","French rule was resisted from the start, by Ho Chi Minh among others.","It's the background to the Vietnam wars."),
"First Sino-Japanese War": ("W",3,"Japan crushed China and became Asia's leading power.","The two fought over influence in Korea. Japan's modern navy destroyed China's fleet.","China ceded Taiwan and paid huge indemnities.","It shocked China and showed Japan's modernization had worked."),
"Japan takes Taiwan": ("P",2,"Taiwan became Japan's first colony.","China ceded Taiwan after its defeat.","Japan ruled for 50 years, building railways and schools.","Taiwan's relatively warm view of Japan contrasts with Korea's."),
"US takes Philippines": ("PW",2,"The US bought the Philippines and fought a brutal war to keep it.","After beating Spain, the US paid $20 million for the islands. Filipino independence fighters resisted; at least 200,000 civilians died.","The Philippines became independent in 1946.","It's a forgotten US colonial war."),
"Boxer Rebellion": ("WR",2,"An anti-foreign uprising besieged Beijing's embassies, and eight nations crushed it.","The Boxers killed missionaries and Chinese Christians. Empress Dowager Cixi backed them. Troops from eight nations broke the siege.","China paid huge reparations; the Qing fell 11 years later.","It deepened Chinese anger at foreign interference."),
"Japan defeats Russia": ("WP",3,"An Asian nation beat a European empire for the first time in modern war.","Japan attacked Russia's base at Port Arthur and destroyed its fleet at Tsushima.","Russia faced revolution at home; Japan took Korea.","It inspired anti-colonial leaders from India to Egypt."),
"Young Turk Revolution": ("P",2,"Reformist officers forced the sultan to restore the constitution.","Young Turk officers demanded a modern Ottoman state.","They later led the empire into WWI on Germany's side.","Mustafa Kemal (Atatürk) came from this movement."),
"Japan annexes Korea": ("P",3,"Korea became a Japanese colony for 35 years.","Japan formally annexed Korea, banned Korean in schools and forced Koreans to take Japanese names.","Korea was freed only in 1945, then divided.","It still poisons Japan-Korea relations."),
"Qing dynasty falls": ("P",3,"China's last dynasty fell, ending 2,000 years of emperors.","An army mutiny in Wuchang spread; the six-year-old emperor Puyi abdicated, and a republic was declared.","China split among warlords.","Both mainland China and Taiwan honor Sun Yat-sen as the founder of modern China."),
"Sykes-Picot Agreement": ("P",3,"Britain and France secretly split up the Middle East.","Diplomats Mark Sykes and François Georges-Picot drew lines dividing Ottoman Arab lands, while Britain also promised Arabs independence.","After WWI, Britain took Iraq and Palestine; France took Syria and Lebanon.","It remains a symbol of Western betrayal in the Arab world."),
"May Fourth Movement": ("IP",2,"Students protested in Beijing, and modern Chinese nationalism was born.","The Versailles treaty gave Germany's rights in China to Japan. Students marched and boycotted Japanese goods.","The Chinese Communist Party was founded in 1921.","China celebrates May 4 as Youth Day."),
"Atatürk's Turkish Republic": ("PI",3,"Atatürk built a secular Turkish republic from the Ottoman ruins.","Mustafa Kemal defeated the Allies' plans to partition Turkey, then abolished the sultanate and caliphate, gave women the vote and adopted the Latin alphabet.","Turkey became a model of secular modernization in the Muslim world.","Atatürk's image is still everywhere in Turkey."),
"Chinese Civil War begins": ("W",3,"China's Nationalists and Communists went to war.","Chiang Kai-shek turned on his Communist allies, massacring them in Shanghai. Mao retreated to the countryside.","The war paused to fight Japan, then resumed; the Communists won in 1949.","It's why there are two Chinas today: the PRC and Taiwan."),
"Gandhi's Salt March": ("PI",3,"Gandhi walked 240 miles to make salt, and shook the British Empire.","Britain taxed salt and banned Indians from making it. Gandhi led a march to the sea and picked up salt, inspiring mass civil disobedience.","Over 60,000 were arrested.","His nonviolent methods inspired MLK, Mandela and many others."),
"Japan seizes Manchuria": ("WP",2,"Japan's army staged a bombing to seize Manchuria.","Japanese officers blew up a railway and blamed China, then took Manchuria and set up the puppet state Manchukuo.","The League of Nations condemned it; Japan simply left.","It showed the League couldn't stop aggression."),
"Japan invades China": ("W",3,"Japan launched full-scale war on China, starting WWII in Asia.","Japan captured Shanghai and Nanjing, where troops massacred tens of thousands of civilians.","China fought on for eight years; about 15–20 million Chinese died.","The Nanjing Massacre is still a bitter issue between China and Japan."),
"Japan attacks Pearl Harbor and SE Asia": ("W",3,"In one day Japan attacked the US, Britain and the Dutch across the Pacific.","Japan struck Pearl Harbor, the Philippines, Malaya and Hong Kong. Singapore fell in February 1942.","The war became truly global.","The fall of Western colonies to Japan helped end European empire in Asia."),
"Hiroshima & Nagasaki": ("WS",3,"Two atomic bombs destroyed two cities and ended WWII.","The US dropped atomic bombs on Hiroshima and Nagasaki, killing over 100,000 people immediately. Japan surrendered.","The nuclear arms race began.","Nuclear weapons have not been used in war since."),
"India & Pakistan partition": ("PRW",3,"British India was split in two, and up to a million people died.","Britain drew borders in weeks dividing Hindu-majority India and Muslim-majority Pakistan. About 15 million people fled across the new borders amid massacres.","The two fought over Kashmir immediately.","India and Pakistan are now nuclear-armed rivals."),
"Israel founded": ("PRW",3,"Israel was declared, and war with its neighbors followed.","As Britain left Palestine, Ben-Gurion declared Israel. Arab states invaded; Israel won. About 700,000 Palestinians fled or were expelled.","Palestinians call it the Nakba (catastrophe).","The Israeli-Palestinian conflict remains unresolved."),
"People's Republic of China": ("PI",3,"Mao declared a communist China.","Mao's Communists won the civil war; the Nationalists fled to Taiwan.","China became communist, with famines and purges under Mao.","The PRC is now the world's second-largest economy."),
"Korean War": ("W",3,"The Cold War turned hot in Korea and the peninsula stayed divided.","North Korea invaded the South; a US-led UN force pushed back; China intervened.","It ended in 1953 without a peace treaty.","Korea is still split by the world's most fortified border."),
"Dien Bien Phu; Vietnam split": ("WP",3,"Vietnamese forces defeated France, and Vietnam was split in two.","The Viet Minh surrounded a French base with artillery hauled up mountains by hand. The French surrendered.","At Geneva, Vietnam was divided; the US backed the South.","It led directly to America's Vietnam War."),
"Great Leap Forward": ("PE",3,"Mao's push to industrialize overnight caused the deadliest famine in history.","Peasants were forced into communes and ordered to make steel in backyard furnaces. Officials exaggerated harvests while grain was exported.","About 30 million people died.","It was hidden for decades and is still sensitive in China."),
"Cultural Revolution": ("PIC",3,"Mao unleashed students to attack 'old ideas', and China descended into chaos.","Red Guards humiliated teachers, destroyed temples and persecuted 'class enemies'.","Schools closed for years; hundreds of thousands to millions died.","Xi Jinping was sent to the countryside during it."),
"Six-Day War": ("WP",3,"Israel defeated three Arab armies in six days.","Israel struck Egypt's air force, then took Sinai, Gaza, the West Bank, East Jerusalem and the Golan Heights.","Israel's occupation of the West Bank and Golan continues.","It's the root of today's settlement disputes."),
"Yom Kippur War; oil embargo": ("WE",3,"Egypt and Syria surprised Israel, and Arab states turned oil into a weapon.","Egypt and Syria attacked on Judaism's holiest day. Arab oil producers embargoed the US and others.","Oil prices quadrupled; Egypt later made peace with Israel in 1979.","It showed the world's dependence on Middle Eastern oil."),
"Saigon falls; Khmer Rouge": ("WP",3,"Vietnam was unified under communism, and Cambodia fell to a genocidal regime.","North Vietnamese tanks rolled into Saigon. In Cambodia, the Khmer Rouge emptied cities and killed up to 2 million people.","Vietnam invaded Cambodia in 1978 to topple the Khmer Rouge.","Cambodia's 'killing fields' are a memorial to the genocide."),
"Deng's market reforms": ("EP",3,"Deng opened China to markets, beginning the greatest economic boom in history.","Deng let farmers sell surplus crops and opened special economic zones like Shenzhen to foreign investment.","Hundreds of millions escaped poverty over the next 40 years.","China became the 'world's factory'."),
"Iranian Revolution; USSR invades Afghanistan": ("PRW",3,"Iran became an Islamic Republic, and the USSR invaded Afghanistan, in the same year.","Khomeini's movement toppled the Shah. Soviet troops invaded Afghanistan to prop up a communist government.","Political Islam spread, and the Afghan war drew Islamist fighters.","Both shaped the Middle East and terrorism for decades."),
"Iran-Iraq War": ("W",2,"Iraq invaded Iran, starting an eight-year war of trenches and gas.","Saddam Hussein hoped to grab land from a weakened revolutionary Iran. Iraq used chemical weapons.","About 500,000 died; the war ended in stalemate.","It shaped Iran's revolutionary identity and Saddam's later invasion of Kuwait."),
"Tiananmen Square": ("PI",3,"China's army crushed pro-democracy protests in Beijing.","Students occupied Tiananmen Square for weeks. On June 4, troops opened fire; hundreds to thousands were killed.","The Party tightened control while pushing economic growth.","The event is censored inside China."),
"Gulf War": ("W",2,"A US-led coalition drove Iraq out of Kuwait.","Saddam Hussein invaded Kuwait. Coalition forces liberated it in 100 hours of ground fighting.","US troops stayed in Saudi Arabia, angering bin Laden.","It opened the era of US dominance in the Gulf."),
"Hong Kong returned; Asian Financial Crisis": ("PE",2,"Britain returned Hong Kong to China, and Asia's economies crashed.","Hong Kong became part of China under 'one country, two systems'. Months later, currencies in Thailand, Indonesia and South Korea collapsed.","The IMF stepped in with bailouts; Indonesia's Suharto fell.","Beijing's 2020 security law ended much of Hong Kong's autonomy."),
"China joins WTO; US invades Afghanistan": ("EW",3,"China joined the global trading system, and the US went to war in Afghanistan.","China's WTO entry opened world markets to Chinese exports. The US invaded Afghanistan after 9/11 and toppled the Taliban.","China's exports boomed; the Afghan war lasted 20 years.","The 'China shock' to factory jobs and the Afghan war both shaped today's politics."),
"Iraq War": ("W",3,"The US toppled Saddam Hussein, unleashing years of war.","The invasion took Baghdad in weeks, but no WMD were found. A sectarian civil war followed.","About 200,000 or more Iraqi civilians died.","Iran's influence grew, and ISIS emerged."),
"Arab Spring; Syria; Fukushima": ("PWS",3,"Uprisings swept the Arab world, Syria fell into war, and Japan suffered a nuclear disaster.","Protests toppled leaders in Tunisia, Egypt and Libya. Syria's crackdown became a civil war. In Japan, a tsunami caused meltdowns at Fukushima.","Syria's war killed about half a million and displaced millions.","Hopes for democracy mostly faded; Syria's Assad finally fell in 2024."),
"Xi Jinping takes power": ("P",3,"Xi Jinping became China's leader and its most powerful since Mao.","Xi became Communist Party leader and soon removed rivals in an anti-corruption campaign.","In 2018 presidential term limits were scrapped.","China grew more assertive abroad and tighter at home."),
"ISIS 'caliphate'": ("WR",2,"ISIS declared a caliphate across Iraq and Syria.","ISIS took Mosul and much of Syria, enslaving and massacring minorities.","A US-led coalition and local forces destroyed the caliphate by 2019.","ISIS offshoots remain active in Africa and Asia."),
"Taliban retake Afghanistan": ("WP",2,"The Taliban took Kabul as US troops withdrew.","The Afghan government collapsed in days.","The Taliban banned girls from secondary school and university.","Afghanistan is the only country barring girls from education past primary school."),
"Oct 7 attack; Gaza war": ("W",3,"Hamas killed about 1,200 people in Israel, and Israel's war on Gaza followed.","Hamas fighters attacked Israeli towns and a music festival, taking about 250 hostages. Israel's military campaign devastated Gaza.","Tens of thousands of Palestinians were killed; the war spread to Lebanon, Yemen and Iran.","It reshaped Middle East politics and global debates."),
}
